## Ops traps (this project's known footguns)
<!-- Keep only the ones that apply; delete the rest. These are the generalizable ones. -->
- **Watcher/kill by pattern matches itself** — `pgrep`/`pkill -f "<pattern>"` matches the watcher's own
  command line → never-ending wait or self-kill; use an exact PID, or a pattern absent from the watcher
  (`[b]ackfill` bracket trick for grep). [L-030]
- **Bulk LLM / API calls throttle** — mass calls (especially alongside a scheduled pipeline) fail in
  bursts; make the script idempotent + retry spaced across passes, run at idle. [L-030]
